[Music]  2016 is coming to a close which means  it's time to leave video game land  behind and spend the holidays with  Grandma December was home to both the  game awards and PlayStation experience  so we got plenty of new trailers and  announcements and some more far more  memorable than others let's get to the  top 10 stories shall we number 10  uncharted 4 story dlc if you thought  naughty dog was done with uncharted 4  you'd be wrong The Lost Legacy is a  standalone story chapter one that the  developer says is shorter than uncharted  for itself but longer than the last of  us is left behind expansion Chloe Fraser  was strangely absent from the most  recent game but she na Dean are taking  the reins this time as the reveal  trailer showed them exchanging fists  with some military guards will  definitely be hearing more about this  lost chapter soon number 9 knack to  announced speaking of games you thought  were finished knack is coming back with  a sequel that you probably weren't  asking for designer mark cerny said  there's a lot of room to explore in that  world and if the reveal trailer is  anything to go by part of that  exploration means playing the game in  coop no release date was given but  nacked two will likely be headed  exclusively to ps4 number 8 pewdiepie's  deleted channel when it comes to YouTube  there's no name bigger than PewDiePie  his videos were already some of the most  popular on the site but the youtuber  vowed to delete his entire channel if he  reached 50 million subscribers then he  hit that milestone and true to his word  PewDiePie deleted his channel except it  wasn't his primary channel but rather an  alternate account with far less views  and subscribers that Swede is an expert  troll number 7 death strandings new  trailer the gaming world loves Hideo  Kojima but more than that they love  dissecting his trailers new footage at  PSX revealed both Guillermo del Toro and  mads mikkelsen and game plus a bunch of  shots of baby dolls and tanks and weird  pinnacles kijima later said the trailer  was full of quote various hints and  this leads so the internet started  digging through the footage again at  this point we should probably just wait  for some real gameplay details number  six marvel vs capcom infinite revealed  you should know by now that a lot of  games were announced at PSX and you can  add marvel vs capcom infinite to the  list the debut footage looked gorgeous  as Ryu Mega Man Iron Man and miss marvel  all duked it out on a rooftop a second  trailer also confirmed captain america  and more again for the roster the  fighter is coming to ps4 xbox one and pc  sometime in 2017 but if you can't wait  until then Ultimate Marvel vs. Capcom 3  is available at a reduced price on ps4  right now number five Super Mario runs  bittersweet launch the most famous video  game character is on one of the most  popular mobile devices in the world so  super mario run should be a win-win  right analyst group super data even  predicted it would make 60 million  dollars in its first month but super  mario runs launched wasn't too hot it  tops 10 million downloads on day one but  the ten dollar price tag and always  online requirement were not very well  received as of this video the game is  sitting at a two-and-a-half star rating  nintendo shares fell and super data  lowered its projection to only 15  million in the first month sorry Mario  number 4 remastered PlayStation classics  speaking of games coming to new  platforms a whole batch of PlayStation  classics are making their way to ps4 we  already knew that the crash bandicoot  games were being remastered but we got  our first look at the insane trilogy at  PSX on the same stage sony also  announced the wipeout omega collection  plus ps4 remasters for Parappa the  rapper patapon and loco roco you've got  to be a fan of at least one of those and  now you'll be able to play the  definitive version number three more  nintendo switch games announced Nintendo  had its own list of games to announce  too we already knew that Zelda breath of  the wild in lego city undercover we're  coming to the switch but that's not all  Dragon Quest 11 has also been confirmed  for the system and banjo kazooie  spiritual successor ukele  Lee has been canceled on Wii U in favor  of a switch version to indie games  seasons of heaven and the sacred hero  are both coming in 2018 and it's just a  few short weeks until Nintendo's big  switch live stream where we'll hear even  more about the official launch lineup  number 2 all the holiday events it is  that time of year and video games all  over have been getting into the holiday  spirit destiny's the dawning  reintroduces the sparrow racing league  street fighter 5 has new holiday  costumes hit man's paris map has been  updated with christmas trees and new  targets the list just goes on and on and  of course gamespot's own game of the  year overwatch got a batch of new  costumes sprays voice lines and all  sorts of presence with the winter  wonderland update it really is the most  wonderful time of the year number 1 The  Last of Us sequel confirmed we're going  back to PSX with this one the last of us  can certainly stand on its own but  Sony's showcase ended with the reveal of  the last of us part 2 Ellie's all grown  up joel is getting up there and that's  really all we know the game is in very  early stages of development after all  but the team at Naughty Dog is loaded  with master storytellers so we expect  big things no release window has been  given but don't be surprised to see this  coming exclusively to ps4 and those are  the biggest stories of December with  that we're closing out the year join us  in 2017 for more video game news reviews  gameplay videos and anything else you  could want from all of us here at  gamespot we hope you had a happy holiday  and a great new year  you  [Music]  you

